course: dictionary
lesson: 12073
title: Words about work and church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning fits. Read the whole sentence, then ask: what kind of place or person is this about?
explain: «Mum has a clerical job. She types letters and files papers at the office.» The words office, typing and files are the clues. So clerical has to do with office work.
explain: «The vicar wore a white clerical collar on Sunday.» A vicar is a church leader, so the clues point to church life. Here, clerical means to do with priests and ministers.
fact: Clerical means to do with office work, such as typing, filing and keeping records.
fact: «Clerical» can also mean to do with the clergy, who are priests, vicars and ministers.
fact: A «clerical error» is a small mistake in writing or typing records, such as a wrong date.
fact: A «clerical collar» is the white collar some priests and ministers wear. People sometimes call it a dog collar.
fact: To check the meaning, put it into the sentence. Does the meaning still make sense? Then you have it.
exercise: «The bill had a clerical error, so the date was wrong.» What is a clerical error here? | Something very old | *A small mistake in writing or typing records | A loud noise in a church | A mistake made while swimming
exercise: «The vicar wore a white clerical collar on Sunday.» What does clerical mean here? | To do with office filing | *To do with priests, vicars and church work | To do with sport | To do with cooking
exercise: «The clerical staff answered the phone and filed the forms.» Who are the clerical staff? | Gardeners | Church choir singers | *Office workers who keep records | Football players
test: «Mum's clerical job means she types letters and files papers.» What kind of work is this? | Sport | Cooking | *Office work | Building
test: «The clerical collar showed he was a minister.» What does clerical mean in this sentence? | *To do with clergy and church work | Dangerous | To do with office filing | Very old
exam: «Dad made a clerical error on the form, writing the wrong year.» What is a clerical error? | *A small mistake in writing or typing records | A broken window | A big storm | A happy song
